[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded scalar compose-values reporting

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CTRL-COMPOSE-VALUES-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Generated syntax and ordered scalar values
STATEMENT: >>>
The reporting interpreter shall recognize compose NAME values EXPR... through
the generated grammar and create a real local vector from one finite scalar
per expression, in physical expression order. Binary operators remain part of
an expression; optional separating commas shall preserve expression boundaries.
It shall not silently concatenate nonscalar vectors or implement sweep forms
through an unrelated approximation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CTRL-BOUND-DIFFERENCE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bound-name subtraction preserves arithmetic precedence
STATEMENT: >>>
When a reporting expression contains an otherwise unresolved hyphenated token
composed solely of bound real names, numeric constants and subtraction, the
interpreter shall reuse generated arithmetic tokens before expression parsing
so division and power retain their declared precedence. Exact bound vector
names shall take priority over this fallback. Voltage and current probe terminal
spellings shall not be split into arithmetic operands. Unknown operands and
over-budget token sequences shall remain refused.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The unchanged qualification fixture first failed unknown_control_vector:gold-1.
An atom-level fallback was rejected because it changed vals/gold-1 into
vals/(gold-1). The replacement splices tokens from the existing ANTLR arithmetic
lexer before parsing. Tests retain this precedence counterexample and a
hyphenated voltage node whose component names are also bound vectors. No new
handwritten lexer or broad claim of Nutmeg lexical compatibility is introduced.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation candidate: ControlExtraction.cs, SpiceParser.g4 and
ControlVectorExecution.cs. Verification candidate: ComposeControlTests in the
syntax and frontend test projects. Initial tests failed before implementation.
Initial verification was refused by the memory guard; subsequent incremental
syntax/frontend regression and a public-client OP/reporting oracle fixture
passed under an explicit 512 MiB process-tree watchdog. See
evidence/control-compose-values.json for scope and measured coverage.
Independent ngspice-47+ experiment produced [-1,3] for values
1 -2 3 and natural/natural/base-ten logarithms for ln/log/log10 respectively.
Raw evidence: E:/Artifacts/Spice-compose-68c67e6. No requirement closure claimed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CTRL-COMPOSE-ATOMIC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Branch ownership and bounded atomic publication
STATEMENT: >>>
Composition shall run only in an active admitted reporting branch, preserve
caller inputs and constants, and replace a local only after every scalar value
has been evaluated successfully. Missing, nonfinite, nonscalar or over-budget
values shall not publish a partial result. The existing 4096-element vector
limit and terminal-reporting analysis boundary shall remain enforced. Reserved
time, frequency and all targets shall be refused by requested preparation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The existing interpreter publishes owned immutable reporting results and never
accesses the filesystem. This addition does not enable inter-analysis control,
complex vectors, compose sweeps or nonlinear behavioral sources. The original
log-functions-1 deck remains unqualified until its physical circuit and all
original assertions execute and agree with ngspice. A targeted wrong-log-base
mutation was detected; full Stryker and long fuzz campaigns are not claimed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CTRL-REAL-LOG-INDEX-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Finite real logarithms and bounded scalar indexing
STATEMENT: >>>
Within admitted real reporting expressions, ln and log shall compute the
natural logarithm and log10 shall compute the base-ten logarithm elementwise.
Nonpositive arguments requiring complex or nonfinite results shall be refused
in this real-only profile. A scalar vector index shall be a finite zero-based
integer inside the vector bounds; fractional, negative and out-of-range indices
shall be refused without truncation or wrapping.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
ComposeControlTests retain the original logarithm regression's independent
gold constants. The OP/reporting qualification fixture exercises the native
assertion exit and the complete admitted operation against ngspice. The
128-case composition property replay is 385,20261111. These reporting semantics
do not implement nonlinear B-source physics, complex logs or index slices.
<<<
